---
// Braces would be Astro expressions, so the JSON sample is a string.
const survivors = `"survivors": [
  { "file": "src/a.ts", "line": 10, "column": 3,
    "mutator": "ConditionalExpression",
    "replacement": "false", "status": "Survived" },
  { "file": "src/b.ts", "line": 6, "column": 2,
    "mutator": "ConditionalExpression",
    "replacement": "false", "status": "Survived" }
]`;
---
<section class="wrap" id="output" aria-labelledby="output-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">/ Output</p>
  <h2 id="output-title">A summary for people. JSON for agents.</h2>
  <p class="lead">Each survivor has the file, line, column, mutator and replacement: enough for an agent to write the missing test and run Reapr again. Reapr reports; your agent writes the missing test. An agent skill for this is coming.</p>
  <div class="pair">
    <figure class="code">
      <figcaption><code>rpr run --diff origin/main</code></figcaption>
      <pre><code>rpr · stryker · diff vs origin/main · 3 ranges in 2 files
